WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.800
Former President

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.434
Donald Trump

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.969
returned to the campaign trail

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.270
in the next few hours

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.639
when he hold a rally in Pennsylvania.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.375
And this hour, his former vice president,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.776
Mike Pence, is holding a campaign

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.877
event in Iowa.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:11.544
CNN's Kyung

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.213
Lah is at that event

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.181
in the town of Nevada.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:15.815
So, Kyung,

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.851
almost all of the GOP candidates

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.619
were in Iowa last night for dinner

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.422
We didn't hear much of a change in tone

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.191
from a lot in the field last night.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.493
So what?

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.695
What are you looking for today?

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.530
Well, we're expecting

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.831
to see the former vice

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.666
president show up just shortly

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:34.834
in the next couple of minutes

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:35.668
or so, Fredricka.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.469
And and really

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.871
what we're going to be looking for

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.738
is to hear

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:42.108
if he indeed does take a different tone

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.110
when it comes to his former

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.445
running mate, Donald Trump.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.179
But as far as what

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.680
Pence is going to be doing here today,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.782
I just want to walk you around.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.350
We're actually in a fire station.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.552
And the people you see seated over here,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.287
these are first responders

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.256
of the Nevada Fire Department.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.458
This is an all volunteer

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.727
fire department with the exception

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.495
of the paid police chief.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.230
And on the docket today,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.131
they're going to be talking about

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.866
public safety issues, issues

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.301
dealing with the local community.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.003
And that's what they're going to be

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.072
focusing their question that's on.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.039
And it's something

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.941
that the former vice president

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.842
would like to talk about.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.011
He wants to talk about these issues

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:18.945
that affect Iowa

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:19.913
caucus members

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:23.416
and try to turn away from Donald Trump,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.418
especially criticism

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.986
directly of Donald Trump.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.521
And I want to explain why.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.055
First, of all,

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:32.826
I want to play some audio of Will Hurd,

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.995
who took on Trump directly at the dinner

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.230
last night. Take a listen.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.333
Donald Trump

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.203
is running to stay out of prison.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.939
And if we elect

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.508
I know, I know.

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.409
I know.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.610
I know.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.778
I know.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.880
Listen, I know the truth.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.150
The truth is hard

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.152
but if we elect Donald Trump,

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.321
we are willingly giving Joe Biden

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:05.125
four more years in the White House.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.794
And inside the room,

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.728
it was

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.730
incredibly loud forks

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.298
for banging on plates.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.333
People were booing,

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.034
heard was essentially booed

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.469
off the stage.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:20.073
So therein lies the conundrum, Fred,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:23.009
because you want to have at least

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.110
if you're Mike Pence,

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.979
you want to peel off those voters,

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.515
you want the support of the Trump base,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.484
but you somehow have to woo them

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.020
and yet criticize

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.954
his former running mate.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.257
It's a very difficult line to thread.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.024
All right.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.759
And we're going to see how he tackles

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:40.927
the environment

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.229
where you are at the fire station today

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.897
when he arrives.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.532
Kyung Lah thank you so much.

